11)the core reason is edge weights, not just data structure.

BFS → works when all edges have equal weight (i.e 1)
Dijkstra → needed when edges have different weights.
So difference is:
BFS
Uses queue
No need to compare distances
First time you reach a node = shortest path
Uses visited

Dijkstra
Uses priority queue
Must compare and update distances
Can revisit nodes with better distance

12) Modulo gives the remainder when one number is divided by another.
   lik a mod m=remainder when a is divided by m 
   Why we use it :- 
-Prevent integer overflow
-Keep numbers within limits
-Required in problems with very large answers
-Makes calculations efficient

Common Mod Value -> 10^9 +7 = 1000000007
Prime number , Fits in integer range, Used in most coding problems
if a < m -> a mod m = a

When to Apply Mod :-
 - After every addition / multiplication in loops
In problems like:
 - DP
 - Graph paths (like Dijkstra count paths)
 - Combinatorics
 as it keeps the numbers small by storing only the remainder.
